            <ArticleTitle>A surgical case of concomitant aneurysms of the brachiocephalic and coronary arteries.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>128-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Brachiocephalic artery aneurysm with concomitant coronary artery aneurysm is rare. We describe a case of a patient with a history of prosthetic graft placement following resection of an abdominal aortic aneurysm and was subsequently found to have a brachiocephalic artery aneurysm. After surgical correction of the brachiocephalic aneurysm, postoperative coronary arteriography demonstrated coronary artery aneurysms, and the patient subsequently underwent coronary artery bypass grafting (CABG).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
